# Build-time settings for the app. Copy to `.env.local` for a local run, or set
# them as build environment variables wherever the site is built.
#
# These reach the browser — Vite substitutes them into the bundle — so nothing
# secret belongs here. The Worker's own secrets (BOARD_TOKEN, ACCESS_*) are set
# with `wrangler secret put` and never appear in this file.

# The Application (client) ID of the Entra ID app registration the board uses to
# reach Microsoft 365 calendars. Set this and connecting a calendar is a single
# button; leave it unset and each person has to bring an app registration of
# their own. Not a credential: a single-page app is a public client, and PKCE —
# not a shared secret — is what proves who is asking. See the README.
# VITE_M365_CLIENT_ID=00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000

# `common` (any work or personal account), `organizations` (work accounts only),
# or your own tenant id to allow nobody else. Defaults to `common`.
# VITE_M365_TENANT=common

# Clerk's publishable key, from your Clerk application's API keys page. Not a
# credential either — same reasoning as VITE_M365_CLIENT_ID above. Leave unset
# and accounts are off entirely: the board runs on local storage plus whatever
# Access or BOARD_TOKEN the Worker has, exactly as it did before Clerk
# existed. See the README's Accounts section for the rest of the setup —
# CLERK_ISSUER is a Worker secret, set with `wrangler secret put`, not here.
# VITE_CLERK_PUBLISHABLE_KEY=pk_live_your-key-here
